## Summary

Implemented `crates/backup/` (P7-04) — full backup creation + restore per ARCHITECTURE.md §13.5 and the §6.2/§6.3/§14.3 behaviour it references.

**What it does**
- **Versioned manifest** (`manifest.rs`): schema-versioned JSON with deterministic ordering; `manifest_sha256_hex` is reproducible across platforms.
- **Atomic export** (`create.rs`): stage with `O_CREAT|O_EXCL` → fsync → **read-back verify (decode + decrypt + re-hash)** → atomic rename; staging file removed on any error.
- **Optional encryption** (`crypto.rs`): Argon2id KDF + XChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD. The §13.1 `backup.encrypted` capability is gated; plaintext backup is **always** allowed per §13.5.
- **Two-phase restore** (`restore.rs`): read-only `plan` (with payload SHA-256 re-verification and Poly1305 auth) + atomic `commit` delegated to `BackupSource::import_snapshot`, whose contract guarantees a failed commit leaves existing data untouched.
- **§6.2 column-faithful** `VerifiedBackup` / `BackupState` / `DestinationKind` so `storage-sqlite` can persist them verbatim.

**I-10(b) sentinels** (plainly commented): `BackupSource` trait (storage-sqlite adapter not yet landed), `AndroidDocument` byte pipe (`ports::platform` being fixed in parallel), payload records (`domain::pack`/`lore`/`conversation`).

**Result**
- `cargo check -p backup`: clean (only an unrelated warning inside `domain`).
- `cargo test -p backup`: **17/17 pass**, including real round-trip, wrong-passphrase rejection, tamper detection, failed-create cleanup, failed-commit atomicity, and §13.5 capability denial.
